---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, currentWork, shelves, articleIdeas } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="site-shell nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">TED JOHNSON <span>WORKS</span></a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#work">Work</a>
        <a href="#shelves">Explore</a>
        <a href="#articles">Stories & Articles</a>
        <a href="https://thelightinthewindowbook.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Book Site</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="hero-panel">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">{site.hero.eyebrow}</p>
            <h1>{site.hero.title}</h1>
            <p class="hero-lede">{site.hero.subtitle}</p>
            <p><span class="highlight"><strong>Useful first. Commercial second.</strong></span></p>
            <div class="actions">
              <a class="button button-gold" href="#work">Explore the Work</a>
              <a class="button button-light" href="https://thelightinthewindowbook.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start With the Story</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-art" aria-label="Ted Johnson Works monogram">
            <div class="hero-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="hero-monogram" aria-hidden="true">TJ</div>
            <p class="hero-caption">Author · Technologist · Teacher · Builder</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cred-strip" aria-label="Ted Johnson background">
          <div><strong>Decades in Technology</strong><span>Hands-on work, testing, support and problem solving</span></div>
          <div><strong>Teacher & Practical Guide</strong><span>Plain-English help designed for real people</span></div>
          <div><strong>Author & Builder</strong><span>Books, tools, stories and projects built from experience</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">AVAILABLE NOW</p>
          <h2>Start with what Ted has built already.</h2>
          <p>Books, practical technology and direct help — with clear paths to the places where each one is available.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-grid">
          {currentWork.map((item) => (
            <article class="card">
              <p class="tag">{item.category.toUpperCase()}</p>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.description}</p>
              {item.highlight && <p><span class="highlight"><strong>{item.highlight}</strong></span></p>}
              <div class="card-actions">
                <a class="button button-gold" href={item.primaryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{item.primaryLabel}</a>
                {item.secondaryUrl && (
                  <a class="secondary-link" href={item.secondaryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{item.secondaryLabel} →</a>
                )}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="shelves">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">THE FULL WORKSHOP</p>
          <h2>Different subjects. One lifetime of learning by doing.</h2>
          <p>Ted Johnson Works is intentionally broad enough to hold the work that exists today and the work still being built.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="shelf-grid">
          {shelves.map((shelf) => (
            <article class="shelf" id={shelf.id}>
              <p class="eyebrow">{shelf.label}</p>
              <h3>{shelf.title}</h3>
              <p>{shelf.description}</p>
              <p class="status">{shelf.status}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="dark-section" id="articles">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">FROM TED’S WORKBENCH</p>
          <h2>Stories and useful articles will connect the shelves.</h2>
          <p>Each article can bring search and social traffic into one subject, then naturally introduce readers to another part of Ted’s work.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="idea-list">
          {articleIdeas.map((idea) => <li><strong>{idea}</strong></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">TED’S PICKS</p>
          <h2>Things worth paying for.</h2>
          <p>The future recommendation library will cover technology, creator tools, training, martial arts and cooking — but only when a recommendation earns its place.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-grid two">
          <article class="card">
            <p class="tag">HOW RECOMMENDATIONS WORK</p>
            <h3>If I wouldn’t recommend it to a friend, it doesn’t belong here.</h3>
            <p>Some future recommendations may include affiliate links. Those relationships will be identified clearly, and the recommendation comes first.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <p class="tag">COMING NEXT</p>
            <h3>A practical free resource</h3>
            <p>The first free resource will give visitors something genuinely useful to take with them while creating a clean path for future email updates.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="site-shell footer-row">
      <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ted Johnson Works. Built to grow with the work.</p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="https://thelightinthewindowbook.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Light in the Window</a>
        <a href="#main">Back to top</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
